      "id": "ch06",
      "number": 6,
      "file": "06-architectures.qmd",
      "anchor": "ch-architectures",
      "title": "Architecture and the form of the population state",
      "introduction": "Different architectures lead to different operator, characteristic and particle descriptions. Shallow, linear and residual models are presented as distinct mathematical contracts rather than as interchangeable approximations of one architecture.",
