      "file": "07-observable-closure.qmd",
      "anchor": "ch-observable-closure",
      "title": "Observable representations and autonomous closure",
      "introduction": "Suitable current observables can retain the information needed for prediction and support autonomous finite approximations. The chapter moves from information constraints and exact observable calculus through scoped obstructions to a sufficient hierarchy and concrete initialized constructions.",
